The big shirt fits much better.
The assistant is still waiting at the register.
I give the small shirt to her.
"The bigger shirt fits much better," I say.
"I would like to keep it."
"That is perfectly fine," the assistant smiles.
She takes the smaller shirt back.
"May I have your receipt?" she asks.
I give her my receipt from Saturday.
She first scans the receipt and then the new shirt.
"There."
"It does not cost extra," she says.
"Do you want the receipt with you?"
"Yes please," I answer.
She prints a new receipt and gives it to me.
I put the receipt in my wallet and the shirt in my bag.
It was very easy to exchange the shirt.
I say thank you for the help and walk out of the store.
Now I finally have the right clothes for the spring.
